;
; RTLXP7.INF - usb-wdm-free RTL815X: Realtek USB Ethernet in vendor mode,
; Windows XP, XP x64, Vista and 7, x86 and x64, for the chips Realtek's own
; XP to 7 drivers do not serve (owner, 2026-10-27; ethernet.md sections 1
; item 8 and 7.6). RTL815X.INF is the Windows 2000 INF and RTL81598.INF
; the Windows 98 SE and ME INF. Written from the Windows 2000 DDK network
; guide's INF pages; no DDK sample INF was read.
;
; Models, one section per system (owner, 2026-10-27):
;   [Models]                  none: 2000, which ignores decorations, has
;                             RTL815X.INF.
;   NTx86.5.1, NTamd64.5.2    XP and XP x64: the RTL8153D (0BDA:8053),
;                             the RTL8156 and 8156B (0BDA:8156, and
;                             0BDA:8056 for the 8156B), the
;                             RTL8157 (0BDA:8157) and the RTL8159
;                             (0BDA:815A).
;   NTx86.6.0, NTamd64.6.0    Vista: as XP.
;                             From 2026-11-07 (owner) also the RTL8157's
;                             0BDA:8057 and A157, the RTL8159's 0BDA:805A
;                             and A15A and ASUS 0B05:1D91, and the RTL8156
;                             and 8156B rebrands Realtek's 7 INF names by
;                             chip (2001:B302, 056E:4017, 065F:3200,
;                             0DF4:0025, 310E:0062, 2D01:0032, 2BAF:0012,
;                             0B05:18D1); Realtek's XP and Vista INFs list
;                             none of them.
;   NTx86.6.1, NTamd64.6.1    7: the RTL8157 and RTL8159 only (with the
;                             ids above). Realtek's 7 driver in
;                             usb-wdm-nonfree lists 0BDA:8053, 0BDA:8156,
;                             0BDA:8056 and the 8156 and 8156B rebrands.
;   NTx86.6.2, NTamd64.6.2    none: Windows 8 and later have no NDIS 5
;                             (ethernet.md section 4.1).
; The RTL8152 and RTL8153 ids (0BDA:8050, 8152, 8153, 8155 and every
; rebrand) are never listed here: usb-wdm-nonfree's Realtek INFs list them
; on XP to 7, and STAGE.TXT allows one INF per id per system. The ids are
; those of Linux r8152.c at f47d2236 for these chips: 0BDA:8053 came into
; its table with the RTL8153C and RTL8153D. Realtek's XP and Vista INFs do
; not list it. Linux names no rebrand's chip; the rebrands here (owner,
; 2026-11-07) are those Realtek's 7 INF (7.61.20) or its Windows 10 INF
; (10.68.20, read for ids and chip sections only) puts in an RTL8156,
; 8156B, 8157 or 8159 section; the id only is taken.
; 0BDA:8056 is the one id here not from Linux: Realtek's own Windows 7
; INF (7.61.20, in usb-wdm-nonfree) lists it in its RTL8156B sections, and
; its XP and Vista INFs do not (owner, 2026-11-06; the id only is taken).
; No device on it has been seen. 7 is left to Realtek's driver. The chip is
; read from its id register, so the id needs no chip path of its own.

[Version]
Signature="$Windows NT$"
Class=Net
ClassGUID={4D36E972-E325-11CE-BFC1-08002BE10318}
Provider=%Provider%
DriverVer=11/06/2026,0.2.1.0

